# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ONLY build output this project produces is build/bin/soundboard.exe.
# Keeping one output location matters: a stale binary somewhere else is
# indistinguishable from a fresh one, and running the wrong copy is a confusing
# failure to diagnose.
build/bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
/dist/

# Wails writes a Windows resource object into the project root during `wails
# build` and removes it on success — an interrupted or failed build leaves it
# behind, where it is otherwise committable.
*.syso

# build/ also holds PACKAGING INPUTS (appicon.png, windows/icon.ico, the
# manifest) which ARE source and must stay tracked. Only build/bin/ above is
# output, so do not broaden this to build/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wails regenerates the JS bindings and runtime on every build. Nothing in the
# shipped code references them (the binary embeds frontend/dist), and they are a
# verbatim copy of upstream Wails rather than this project's source — so
# committing them would create an attribution obligation for no benefit.
frontend/wailsjs/

# The vanilla frontend under frontend/dist IS source — hand-written HTML/CSS/JS
# with no build step. Never ignore it.
!frontend/dist/
!frontend/dist/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
vendor/
*.test
*.out
*.prof
coverage.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The clip library
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User-supplied and never committed. No audio ships with this project, and PRs
# adding audio are declined (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `sounds/` matches at ANY depth and
# would silently untrack internal/catalog/testdata/sounds/, which the catalog
# tests depend on. Root-anchored, it matches only the library.
/sounds/

# Scratch from importing or fetching clips.
*.part
.raw_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient verification screenshots use the _name.png convention.
_*.png

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
